The geometry of the differential arises, naturally enough, from tangent lines and planes. 
(See Figures 4.6 and 4.7)
In particular, the incremental change Δf measures the change in the height of the graph of f when moving from a to a + h; the differential change df measures the corresponding change in the height of the graph of the (hyper)plane tangent to the graph at a. 
When ||h|| is small (i.e., when a + h is close to a). 
